#: admin-content.php:48
msgid "Some minor tweaks to make WordPress a bit more appealing to bloggers and single-user site owners."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:71
msgid "If not used properly, post tags can create a lot of duplicate content in your site. This feature hides them and redirects tag archives to your homepage."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:75
msgid "If you are not using post formats, they only add clutter to the post editor."
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:86
msgid "Disable attachment pages"
msgstr ""

#: quevedo.php:87
msgid "WordPress can create a page for each uploaded file, which adds a lot of thin content. This feature redirects those pages to the file itself, as WordPress does by default on sites created with version 6.4 or later."
msgstr ""
